# Display precision (two decimals)

## Rule

Every **user-facing** number must display with **exactly two decimal places** (e.g. `12.30`, `0.00`).

Do **not** drop decimals for whole numbers. Do **not** use `toFixed(0|1|3)` (or equivalent) in UI.

Non-finite values → show `—`.

## Applies to

- Live / generic data overlays
- Friction / force analysis overlays
- Status bar text that embeds numbers
- 3D force / velocity / scalar labels
- Chart current readouts (title-side values)
- Param slider current values

## Does NOT apply to

- Physics `tick` / integration / internal accumulators
- Chart **history sample storage** (only the displayed readout is two decimals)

## Implementation

- Use shared helper `formatQuantity(n: number): string` (preferred path: `src/utils/formatQuantity.ts`)
- All display sites must call that helper (or identical `toFixed(2)` + non-finite guard)
- Spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-11-display-and-mechanics-rules-design.md`
